A||||7||loafer87gt||300 HP 3.1||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-21-2000||10:47 PM||||Hi guys,<P>Just got back from the car show here in sunny ol' Saskatoon and I saw something that might interest the crew. A guy had a older cavalier with an aluminum 3.1 running 11.4:1 compression putting out 296 HP. I thought this was a load of BS until he showed me his dyno sheets! Very impressive little package. He said the biggest gains were in the custom aluminum splayed heads he had made for the engine. He also had a custom ram air conversion from a newer grand am on his ride. I didn't like the car too much, but the engine looked real trick. I'll see if I can get a list of parts from him that he used in his rebuild. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||04-21-2000||11:04 PM||||I just can't help but wonder, why would you want 300 H.P. in a Cavalier???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sleeper||04-21-2000||11:13 PM||||HEADS MAKE THE MOTOR.||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||04-22-2000||03:30 PM||||My thoughts exactly. Can you imagine the torque steer on the car! It would be pretty much undriveable! I know in my brothers 170+HP civic it is really difficult to get a good launch without the car pulling or sliding to the right. Double this amount of power and you'd have some serious problems.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-22-2000||04:34 PM||||Big horsepower gains with the right heads, too bad we have very limited choices.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||04-22-2000||06:30 PM||||Big heads = big HP and big HP= big (swelled ) heads||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||04-22-2000||08:09 PM||||I see and drive cars with those numbers a lot and if the owner/builder does it right you WILL be able to drive the car all the time without hateing the car... proper suspension mods and a little discipline and their not that bad...   The most recent additon to the shops go list is a S/C GS-R with 14psi m90, 8.2:1 comp laying 293hp at the wheels! it was TOTALY useless until he put in a LSD.. now its the perfect daily driver... My Alfa nearly that and it's BONE STOCK... (well, Remus exhaust and K&N filter)  170 in a Civic? He have an SI? or B18 swap? Big numbers also mean big money... with a bank roll to support those numbers your allowed a slightly larger head then most others... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||04-22-2000||08:19 PM||||At what RPM? Want more HP? Keep winding it.||||reg||1
